### ============================================================
### HTTP test file — open in IntelliJ and click the green arrows.
### inventory-service runs on 8082. Run these AFTER your app starts.
### The concurrency test (Checkpoint D) is in the README — it needs a
### terminal, because this file runs requests one at a time.
### ============================================================

### 1. Create inventory for product 1 -> expect 201 Created + Location header
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "description": "87-key TKL, brown switches",
  "price": 4999.00,
  "availableQty": 10
}

### 2. Create INVALID inventory -> expect 400 with fieldErrors populated
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": null,
  "name": "",
  "price": -5,
  "availableQty": -1
}

### 3. Create for the SAME productId again -> expect 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "name": "Duplicate on purpose",
  "price": 100.00,
  "availableQty": 1
}

### 4. Get by productId -> expect 200, reservedQty = 0
GET http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/1

### 5. Get a productId with no inventory -> expect 404, not 500
GET http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/99999

### 6. List all
GET http://localhost:8082/api/inventory

### 7. Reserve 3 of product 1 -> expect 200, availableQty 7, reservedQty 3
###    Then check the DB: version should have gone from 0 to 1.
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 3
}

### 8. Reserve MORE than available -> expect 409 (or 422), InsufficientStock message
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 1000
}

### 9. Reserve with an invalid quantity -> expect 400 with fieldErrors
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 0
}

### 10. Reserve for a product with no inventory -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory/reserve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 99999,
  "quantity": 1
}

### 11. Seed for Checkpoint D: a product with exactly ONE unit
POST http://localhost:8082/api/inventory
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 2,
  "name": "Last Unit Lamp",
  "description": "only one left — used for the race test",
  "price": 1299.00,
  "availableQty": 1
}
